hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1220","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Haywa told us, that Al-Walid bin Abi Al-Walid told him, that Ayoub bin Khaled bin Abi Ayyub Al-Ansari told him, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Keep the engagement. Then perform ablution, and perform your ablution well, then pray what God has ordained for you, then praise your Lord and glorify Him, then say: O God, You are able, but I am not able. And You know and I do not know, and You are the Knower of the unseen, so if you deem something good for me in so-and-so, and you call it by her name, in my religion, in this world, and in my hereafter, then ordain it for me. And if something else is better for me than it in my religion, this world, and the hereafter, then settle it for me, or he said: Determine it for me.”"
